WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.235
[dramatic music]

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.803
 Jesse, Teddy, congratulations.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.405
You boys have made it
into the final round

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.773
of this competition.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.275
Now when you showed up here, we
had you make fossil Damascus.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.111
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:15.548
to recreate something with a
little bit more recent history.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.682
This.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.985
[dramatic music]

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:20.786
This is a musketeer's rapier.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.223
[sighing]

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.625
 Oh, dear.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.893
I told my wife before I
left, the one weapon I did

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:29.295
not want to build was a rapier.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.965
Yeah.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:33.966
 Good luck, gentlemen.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:34.868
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:35.567
 Oh, we're screwed.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.436
 I'm speechless.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:37.937
 Good luck.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:38.705
 Holy crap.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.810
 It's day one.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.080
And I get to build
the musketeer rapier.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.948
So I'm using 5160.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:49.749
It's tough.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.950
It's springy.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.619
Rapiers, since
they're so thin, they

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.086
are meant to flex a little bit.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.222
So that's what we're going.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.057
So today, my game
plan is to hopefully

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.092
get the blade roughed out.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.527
That will allow
me to spend a lot

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.097
of time working on the
guard, making it elaborate.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.132
But right now, I'm really
glad I have long arms.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.666
I'd love to give
the judges something

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:11.771
that they want to stare at
just so much they want to use.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.472
I've got the entire
blade shaped.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.641
It's beveled.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.476 line:7%
I'm satisfied with where I'm at.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:23.182
 Day one, and I'm taking
on the musketeer rapier.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:27.087
I'm going to go with bar
stock size of 80CrV2.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:30.289
Super strong, should hold
up very well to the testing.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.024
That's going to be the
hardest part because I don't

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.626
know what it has to survive.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.128
Hey.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.396
I'm about 40 and 1/2 inches
total length, which gives

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.165
me plenty of room for error.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.767
I think I'm going to start
working on the fuller.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:45.238
[rock music]

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.343
I can't complain about
that, my first ever fuller.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:53.312
With all the factors involved
in this quench, the low roof

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.116
of the garage, the tall
quench tank, a ladder just

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.285
to reach above it--

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:02.522
I'm hoping that I can get
it right the first time.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.391
[dramatic music]

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.592
God damn it.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:09.328
Catastrophically, the sword
drops out of my hands.

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:12.064
I hear the tip hit the
bottom of the tank.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.867
I pull the sword
out of the quench.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.535
I see this huge bow.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:19.204
I gotta get this thing
in my straightening jig.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:21.006
I have no idea what's
going to come out.

00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:21.875
I'm really scared.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.409
I'm really nervous.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:26.279
I'm thinking I'm going to
have to do this a second time.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.781
So the sword's cooled off
in the straightening jig.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.417
Let's see if I just
performed a miracle here.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.654
It's time to open it up
and see what's inside.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.390
Holy crap.

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:40.627
There's a slight warpage on
there, but nothing crazy that I

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.428
can't fix with a grinder.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.796
She's hard.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.299
I've never made a store before,
so I'm ecstatic right now.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.271
 The plan for the day is I
gotta get the blade and rough

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.274
ground and heat treated.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.243
This thing is so freaking long.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.945
And then it'll be onto all
the fittings and furnishings.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:03.383
[rock music]

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.152
It's not biting.

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:07.553
It's not skating quite right.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.822
I realize I have to requench,
I have to reharden this.

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.791
I just want to make sure that
when it gets to the judges,

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.693
it's going to survive
whatever they throw at it.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:17.430
I haven't seen any warps.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:20.599
So that is without a doubt hard.

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.534
It's still a little
bit beefy compared

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:26.906
to what I wanted in the long
run, but I'm satisfied with it.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.043 line:0%
 For this handle, I'm going
to go with a nice hardwood

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.445 line:0%
and offset that with a
different color micarta.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.914
And then epoxy it together so I
can shape it off of the sword.

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:36.982
Yeah.

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:38.584
That came together pretty nice.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.887
With the time I got left, I'm
going to started shaping all

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.354
these quillons,
and knuckle-bows,

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.490
and all that frou frou
stuff on the handles.

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:48.895
 I'm really happy
with where I'm at.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.996
The elements I have to get
finished are the knuckle-bow

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:53.700
with two sidebars and a pommel.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.068
There's your knuckle-bow.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.702
The fit and finish that
I'm going to put on it--

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.538
it's going to look rugged
but clean, pretty, and just a

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.273
overall well constructed piece.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.209
$10,000 worthy, no doubt.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.776
Dry fit up in place.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.112
Looking good.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.446
At the end of the
cross guard, I have

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:10.850
two quillons, dragon
fingers, claws that should

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.919
be clutching a gem or two.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.787
They look dragonesque.

00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:17.690
That's done.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.692
It is a little bit heavy
for what I was aiming for,

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.993
but it has good balance.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.829 line:0%
So overall, I'm really happy
with how the sword turned out.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.432 line:0%
 Today's going to be
all about fit and finish,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:30.069 line:7%
and completing this sword.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.570
The blade itself,
I'm pretty much

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.339
happy with the geometry of it.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:36.008
But I want to see if I can
remove some weight at the tip.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.978
I want Doug to be swinging
that thing all over the place,

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.812
and having a good time with it.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.649
[dramatic music]

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:45.384
Now that everything is
permanently affixed,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.820
just got to clean it up,
sharpen up a little bit.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.989
I can't wait to see the
judges test this thing.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:52.024
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:55.094
Welcome to the kill test.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.395
We're going to
take your rapiers,

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:59.165
and deliver some killing
slashes and thrusts

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.733
on this big carcass.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.234
For these musketeer
swords, it's time

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.436
to find out if you're
all for one champion

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:07.406
or one for all the runner ups.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.373
Jesse, you're up first.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.375
Are you ready for this?

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.209
 Let's cut some bacon.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:11.010
 All right.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:11.977
Let's do this.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:15.448
[rock music]

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:28.695
 Dude.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.663
He got a workout.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:31.864
 All right, Jesse.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.533
This edge is sharp.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.902
A rapier cut a pig in half?

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.604
That's very interesting.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.608
For every slash, the edge lands
exactly where I want it to be.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.675
 OK.

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:46.612
 Overall, sir, for
this test, it will kill.

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.848
 Yes.

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.182
 All right, ready, Teddy?

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.150
 Let's do it.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.884
 Let's do this.

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:56.422
[rock music]

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:13.139
[sighs]

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.711
All right, Teddy, your edge.

00:06:19.811 --> 00:06:21.480
When you're slashing
with the razor's edge

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:24.617
that you have on your
blade, it slices easily

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:27.185
and deeply on this pig carcass.

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:29.789
Your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:30.689
 Awesome.

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.925
Nice.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.893
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test--

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.030
a little thing I like to
call the wheel of pain.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.601
Now a rapier it needs to be a
fast, light, flexible weapon.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:45.304
We're going to see how
flexible yours are.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.173
All right, Jesse, so
I've got your blade

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.342
strapped into our wheel
of pain right now.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.576
Now I'm going to be flexing
it in both directions.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.513
I'll be taking it all the
way to that far red peg,

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.248
holding it for
about three seconds,

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.883
and we'll see if
it comes back true.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.785
And then we're going
the other direction.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:00.720
All right?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.455
 Go nuts.

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.823
 That ship sailed.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:08.194
[dramatic music]

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:49.435
 That was back to true, dude.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:50.937
[applause]

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:52.971
 Are you kidding me?

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:54.573
 OK, Jesse.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.241
First off, remarkable.

00:07:56.308 --> 00:08:00.112
I mean, there's a lot of weight
in this blade, a lot of mass.

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:02.148
So to have it flex
the way it did,

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:04.683
and come back
virtually to true--

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.453
this blade is still straight
enough to fight with,

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:08.420
which is excellent.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:09.155
 Thank you.

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:09.988
 Good job.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.156
 Thank you.

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:12.424
 Teddy, you ready for this?

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:14.025
 Let's do it.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:17.597
[dramatic music]

00:08:27.072 --> 00:08:28.941
Oh, freak.

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:32.245
[dramatic music]

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:36.716
[inaudible]

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:41.987
Holy crap.

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:45.290
 So, Teddy, you can see
where it took the bends here

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:46.625
and here.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.894
In the initial bend, it
actually bent this way.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.597
And then we bent it back, and
then it went the other way.

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:54.900
So it leaves some question
about the heat treat--

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.104
you know, how even it
is through the blade.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.505
You know, it's just--

00:09:00.572 --> 00:09:02.140
I worry about that bend.

00:09:02.207 --> 00:09:05.778
 Teddy, unfortunately, a
less than perfect heat treat

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:08.981
has led to your rapier
taking a permanent bend.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.316
Now this is going
to affect accuracy

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:15.087
when it comes to the use of the
weapon in our sharpness test.

00:09:15.153 --> 00:09:17.790
And for that reason, this
is a catastrophic failure,

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.225
and you cannot continue
with this competition.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:21.193
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.031
 Good job, brother.

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:26.332
 I'm definitely not happy.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:30.069
No one enjoys having anything
they build not work properly.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:31.137
I've had a blast.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:32.505
I've made a few good friends.

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:34.673
I've been able to take
time, and build something

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.874
I otherwise wouldn't
have built. So

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:37.109
that experience has been great.

00:09:40.345 --> 00:09:41.714
 Jesse, congratulations.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:43.649
You are the Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:43.716 --> 00:09:46.452
and that is a title that comes
with a check for 10 grand.

00:09:46.518 --> 00:09:47.820
Good job, brother.

00:09:47.887 --> 00:09:50.556
[applause]

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:52.091
 I'm on cloud nine.

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:56.061
This is probably the most fun
I've ever had doing hard labor.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.663
I've proved to myself that
I'm capable to do a whole lot

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.532
more than I thought I could.

00:10:00.599 --> 00:10:04.003
[dramatic music]

